"""bd-tools -- the map of the toolchain: every bd-* tool, grouped, with a one-liner.

The suite is large (~80 tools); this makes it navigable. Reads each tool's summary
line and prints it under a category. `bd-tools <term>` filters by name/summary.

Usage:
    bd-tools               grouped index
    bd-tools <term>        only tools whose name/summary matches
    bd-tools --bin DIR     scan a different bin (default: <checkout>/toolchain/bin)
Read-only.
Exit 0 = reported; 3 = --check found an uncategorized/stale tool; 2 =
CANNOT-EVALUATE (the --bin directory is absent or holds no bd-* tools -- a count
over an empty denominator is not a report).
"""
